  "notes": [
    "CT-ADF-1, CT-ADF-2: the hand-over names the service, role, exact PFA standard with its fetch date (ADF Careers, fetched 2026-09-23) and the PFA date; the plan peaks for the PFA, not enlistment. CT-ADF-4: targets are 1 shuttle level and about 25% more push-ups and sit-ups than the standard.",
    "CT-ADF-6, CT-ADF-7, CT-ADF-8: push-ups and sit-ups are practised to the exact test technique 3 times a week, stopped 2 to 3 reps short. Use Incline Push Up until the lifter meets the standard. Cadence, time limit and beep-test version: confirm with Defence Force Recruiting.",
    "CT-ADF-11: a mock PFA runs before the program starts (week 0) and replaces week 4's shuttle session; week 4 is also the L-7 deload and the lighter running week (CT-RUN-4).",
    "CT-RUN-4: run volumes are defaults (the easy run grows 25, 30, 35 min, at most 20% a week, then 25). Set them from the lifter's current running; female candidates and novice runners stay at 20% or less a week (CT-ADF-13).",
    "CT-CON-4, CT-RUN-3: hard runs (intervals, shuttle) sit on non-lifting days; nothing fast follows strength work on the same day.",
    "CT-ADF-9: squat, hinge, pull-ups, a lift to a platform (Power Clean) and loaded carries every week. CT-ADF-14: Special Forces candidates need pull-ups 3 times a week, which the 6-day layout gives.",
    "CT-ADF-10: load carriage is optional and not drafted; if added, at most 1 session every 10 to 14 days."
  ]
